<!--
  Main pages sitemap. Each entry carries:
  - <lastmod>           — freshness signal for re-crawl
  - <xhtml:link>        — hreflang self-references and the .com/.in mirror
  - <image:image>       — primary visual for the page (sitelinks eligibility)
  - <changefreq> + <priority> — relative importance for the crawler

  Sitelinks (the "About Us · Services · Partner ·" chips that appear under
  the main brand result in Google) need three things to surface:
  1. A clean, consistent site structure (covered here)
  2. Discoverable internal links from every page (Navigation + Footer)
  3. Enough click data per page that Google trusts it as a destination

  We can't accelerate #3 — it accumulates over months. But this file maxes
  out #1, which makes Google more likely to pick sitelinks when it does.
-->
